    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Not every business can meet the strict listing conditions of the main stock exchange. The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Second Tier Securities Market (SSM)</span> was created to give small and medium-sized, indigenous companies a simpler route to raise long-term capital.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of the SSM</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The SSM is a segment of the capital market designed specifically for small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) that cannot yet satisfy the rigorous requirements of listing on the main/first-tier stock exchange, but still wish to raise capital from the investing public.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Objectives of Establishing the SSM</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Objective</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Encourage SMEs</td><td>Give small, growing, and indigenous businesses access to long-term capital.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reduce entry barriers</td><td>Relax the stringent listing conditions of the main exchange.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Broaden the market</td><td>Increase the number and variety of securities available to investors.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Promote indigenisation</td><td>Support locally owned enterprises to grow and eventually graduate to the main board.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Create employment</td><td>Growth of SMEs financed through the SSM helps generate jobs.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Listing Requirements for Companies on the SSM</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Compared with the main board, SSM listing requirements are less demanding — for example, a lower minimum share capital, a shorter trading history, and a smaller percentage of shares required to be offered to the public. This makes it realistic for younger and smaller companies to qualify.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Role of the SSM in Promoting Indigenous Enterprises</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">The SSM acts as a <strong>stepping stone</strong>: indigenous enterprises that are too small for the main exchange can raise capital, build a track record, and grow — with many eventually migrating to the main/first-tier board once they meet its full requirements.</div>\n",
