    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  No country can develop trade and industry entirely on its own. Nations often form <span class=\"learn-keyword\">economic groupings</span> — associations of countries that cooperate to boost trade, industry, and development within a region.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Economic Grouping</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">An economic grouping is a voluntary association of two or more countries that agree to cooperate in trade, finance, and economic development, usually by removing barriers to trade among members and pursuing common economic goals.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Examples of Economic Groupings in West Africa</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Grouping</th><th>Full Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>ECOWAS</td><td>Economic Community of West African States</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>WAEC</td><td>West African Examinations Council (an educational, not purely economic, body often listed alongside regional institutions)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>MRU</td><td>Mano River Union</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Objectives of ECOWAS</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">Founded in <strong>1975</strong> (Treaty of Lagos), ECOWAS aims to promote cooperation and integration among West African states — creating a common market, free movement of goods, services, capital and people, and ultimately economic union.</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Achievements and Challenges</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Achievements</th><th>Challenges</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>ECOWAS free movement of persons and goods</td><td>Poor road/rail infrastructure linking member states</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Regional peace-keeping (e.g. ECOMOG)</td><td>Political instability in some member countries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Common trade liberalisation scheme</td><td>Multiple currencies and slow monetary integration</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Joint development projects</td><td>Trade barriers and border restrictions still persist in practice</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n",
