    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Business does not operate in a vacuum — it is guided by rules. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Business law</span> is the body of law that governs commercial and business dealings, protecting the interests of everyone involved in trade.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Business Law</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Business law refers to the rules, statutes, and regulations that govern the conduct of people and organisations engaged in commerce, trade, sales, and business dealings generally.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Sources of Business Law</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Legislation (statutes)</td><td>Laws made by the National Assembly or State Houses of Assembly.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Common law</td><td>Law developed from customs and judicial precedents (case law).</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Customary law</td><td>Traditional/customary practices recognised as binding within a community.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Case law/judicial precedent</td><td>Decisions of the courts which guide future similar cases.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of Business Law in Commerce</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">Business law protects both buyers and sellers, enforces agreements, provides a framework for resolving disputes, builds trust in trade, and ensures fair competition in the market.</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Types of Laws Affecting Business</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>What it Covers</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Contract law</td><td>Governs agreements between parties and their enforceability.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Company law</td><td>Governs formation, management, and dissolution of companies.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sale of goods law</td><td>Governs the sale and transfer of ownership of goods between buyer and seller.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Agency law</td><td>Governs relationships where one person (agent) acts on behalf of another (principal).</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n",
