    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Business people often need a safe, convenient way to make large payments without physically carrying cash. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Negotiable instruments</span> are documents that make this possible.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Definition of Negotiable Instruments</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A negotiable instrument is a written, signed document that entitles a person to a specific sum of money, and which can be transferred from one person to another (by delivery or endorsement) so that the new holder can claim the money in their own right.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Negotiable Instruments</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cheque</td><td>A written order by an account holder (drawer) directing their bank to pay a stated sum to a named person or bearer.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Bill of exchange</td><td>A written, unconditional order by one party (drawer) directing another (drawee) to pay a specific sum to a named person or bearer, on demand or at a future date.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Promissory note</td><td>A written, unconditional promise by one person (maker) to pay a specific sum to another (payee) on demand or at a fixed future time.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Features of Negotiable Instruments</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">Must be in <strong>writing</strong>; must be <strong>signed</strong> by the maker/drawer; must specify a <strong>certain sum</strong> of money; must be payable <strong>on demand or at a fixed/determinable future time</strong>; and must be freely <strong>transferable</strong> to another holder.</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance in Business Transactions</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Importance</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Safety</td><td>Reduces the risk of carrying large sums of cash.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Convenience</td><td>Makes settlement of large or distant transactions easier.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Credit facility</td><td>Allows businesses to buy now and pay later (e.g. via bills of exchange).</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Evidence of debt</td><td>Serves as legal proof that a sum of money is owed.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n",
